\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces The future cone $\symcal {F}(x,t_0)$ expands as time increases under non-contracting dynamics. Vertical slices at $t_1$ and $t_2$ show growing reachability sets. The cone boundary $\partial \symcal {F}$ is a smooth hypersurface (\cref {thm:future-cone}). Trajectory collapse corresponds to the cone narrowing to a lower-dimensional submanifold.}}{138}{figure.caption.6}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.1}{\ignorespaces The admissibility manifold $\symcal {A}(x,t)$ (gold) is a proper subset of the reachability set (teal). States in the reachability set but outside the admissibility manifold are \emph {extractive}: reaching them collapses future possibility below threshold $\mitalpha $.}}{150}{figure.caption.10}%
